#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147207 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147570 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64181d45-ac95-5c6c-86bb-407a0a3cb811" :knowledge-point/title "Modeling Exponential Decay Using a Decay Rate"}] :question/id #uuid "34889441-479d-59e6-b9c6-a3972ff9ea60" :question/math-academy-id "e-2068" :question/problem "The number of members $m$ of a club after $t$ years is given by the formula \n\n$$\nm(t) = 766 \\cdot (\\textrm{___})^{t}.\n$$\n\nIf there were $766$ members initially, and the number of members decreases by $22\\%$ each year, what is the missing value in the expression for $m(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for exponential decay (in terms of a decay rate $r$) is\n\n$$\nm(t) = a(1-r)^t.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- $a=766$ is the initial number of members.\n\n- $r = 0.22$ is the decay rate ($22\\%$ expressed as a decimal).\n\n- $t=$ the time, in years.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $m$ is\n\n$$\nm(t)= 766\\cdot (1 - 0.22)^{t} = 766\\cdot (0.78)^{t}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $0.78.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147208 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "873b588f-41f6-561a-99bf-f6764a9338ac" :knowledge-point/title "Modeling Exponential Decay Using a Decay Factor"}] :question/id #uuid "06d40324-f901-5e87-93c1-318a819eb635" :question/math-academy-id "e-2070" :question/problem "A mountain has a glacier with a depth of $75\\,\\textrm{m}.$ The depth of the glacier reduces by $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ every year. Construct a function that represents the depth $d(t)$ of the glacier after $t$ years." :question/worked-solution "The depth of the glacier is $75\\,\\textrm{m},$ and this reduces by $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ every year. Therefore, the depth decays exponentially with a decay factor of $\\dfrac 3 4.$\n\nThe formula for exponential decay (in terms of a decay factor $b$) is\n\n$$\nd(t) = ab^t.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- $a=75 \\textrm{ m }$ is the initial depth of the glacier.\n\n- $b = \\dfrac 3 4$ is the decay factor.\n\n- $t =$  the time, in years.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for the depth $d(t)$ is\n\n$$\nd(t)= 75 \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac 3 4\\right)^{t}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508949 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "873b588f-41f6-561a-99bf-f6764a9338ac" :knowledge-point/title "Modeling Exponential Decay Using a Decay Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32a56108-53b2-53e0-b3aa-7b816128a40c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508465} {:answer/id #uuid "36174f42-7a31-57ce-a2f7-fc99f9926df2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508470} {:answer/id #uuid "cfac9794-90ef-53f2-8ace-d19fb1866019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508720} {:answer/id #uuid "e4479b0b-ed9e-566c-b900-f0e0cabba3d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508754} {:answer/id #uuid "f3e49bb4-a7ca-56cb-8d47-e747459a6da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508786}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36174f42-7a31-57ce-a2f7-fc99f9926df2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508470} :answer-field/id #uuid "97c59463-67ac-5c37-b808-28ec533a2185" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508863}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "87d542d6-aac4-513b-9fc9-107312f9fcdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-61704" :question/problem "Ralf is investigating the effect of a substance on some bacteria. In the beginning, there were $3\\,000$ bacteria. After introducing the substance, Ralf noticed that the number of bacteria reduces by $\\frac{1}{4}$ every minute.\n\nThe function $y(t)$ models the number of bacteria after $t$ minutes and is given by\n\n$$\ny(t)=3\\,000\\cdot {(\\text{___})}^{t}.\n$$\n\nWhat number is missing?" :question/worked-solution "If the number of alive bacteria reduces by $\\frac{1}{4}$ every minute, then $\\frac{3}{4}$ of the bacteria remains every minute. So the decay factor is $\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\nThe formula for exponential decay (in terms of a decay factor $b$) is\n\n$$\ny=a{b}^{t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- $a=3\\,000$ is the initial number of bacteria.\n\n- $b=\\frac{3}{4}$ is the decay factor.\n\n- $t=$ the time, in minutes.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $y(t)$ is\n\n$$\ny(t)=3\\,000\\cdot {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{t}.\n$$\n\nSo the missing number is $\\frac{3}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508944 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147570 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64181d45-ac95-5c6c-86bb-407a0a3cb811" :knowledge-point/title "Modeling Exponential Decay Using a Decay Rate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e827a54-6096-5c80-bba1-693df6b26718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)=5\\,000\\cdot (1.97)^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508574} {:answer/id #uuid "8c60717e-c83d-574a-b40b-5304cef96988" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)=5\\,000\\cdot (1.03)^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508600} {:answer/id #uuid "93358351-2598-53cd-95f8-321fc0f75e71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)=5\\,000\\cdot (0.97)^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508609} {:answer/id #uuid "c3a71056-b38b-5ae1-9295-ea4b98694c2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)=5\\,{000}^{t}\\cdot (0.97)^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508692} {:answer/id #uuid "c904b59d-277d-5b2f-87ed-d1719d7ae5d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)=5\\,000\\cdot (0.03)^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93358351-2598-53cd-95f8-321fc0f75e71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)=5\\,000\\cdot (0.97)^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508609} :answer-field/id #uuid "8da6b427-b2a9-5273-9d5b-a3e0321ac702" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "76eb003d-42ac-559c-8f1c-f5ce54d3972f" :question/math-academy-id "q-61793" :question/problem "The population of a certain animal species is declining at a rate of $3%$ per year. If the species' initial population was $5\\,000$ when the observations started, then which function correctly represents $y(t),$ the population of the species after $t$ years?" :question/worked-solution "The formula for exponential decay (in terms of a decay rate $r$) is\n\n$$\ny(t)=a(1-r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- $a=5\\,000$ is the initial population.\n\n- $r=0.03$ is the decay rate ($3%$ expressed as a decimal).\n\n- $t=$ the time, in years.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $y$ is\n\n$$\ny(t)=5\\,000\\cdot (1-0.03)^{t}=5\\,000\\cdot (0.97)^{t}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508933 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147570 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64181d45-ac95-5c6c-86bb-407a0a3cb811" :knowledge-point/title "Modeling Exponential Decay Using a Decay Rate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fc51612-7335-5405-a867-06bedef88589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1\\,130\\cdot (0.78)^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508414} {:answer/id #uuid "1971332b-98bc-5d82-9a5c-5ade21bcf18c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1\\,130\\cdot (0.98)^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508430} {:answer/id #uuid "9e1e730d-f056-5195-a7a4-c483231ec40c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1\\,130\\cdot (0.88)^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508629} {:answer/id #uuid "cf39f467-3e06-5bbf-a6dd-84f47ff74723" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1\\,130\\cdot (0.12)^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508718} {:answer/id #uuid "d7e5ec68-33d5-5add-8170-e5568b2bb7dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1\\,130\\cdot (0.02)^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e1e730d-f056-5195-a7a4-c483231ec40c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1\\,130\\cdot (0.88)^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508629} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1172f21-48d5-50a2-8bbb-2e078be6a776" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5be49d8c-c7c0-5d12-b018-ff8157121a39" :question/math-academy-id "q-62054" :question/problem "The daily milk production on Debbie's farm has decreased at a rate of $12%$ every month. If the daily milk production was $1\\,130$ liters initially, then which function correctly represents $p(t),$ the daily milk production after $t$ months?" :question/worked-solution "The formula for exponential decay (in terms of a decay rate $r$) is\n\n$$\np(t)=a(1-r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- $a=1\\,130$ is the initial daily milk production.\n\n- $r=0.12$ is the decay rate ($12%$ expressed as a decimal).\n\n- $t=$ the time, in months.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $p$ is\n\n$$\np(t)=1\\,130\\cdot (1-0.12)^{t}=1\\,130\\cdot (0.88)^{t}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508994 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "873b588f-41f6-561a-99bf-f6764a9338ac" :knowledge-point/title "Modeling Exponential Decay Using a Decay Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3af5368a-546f-56e4-bff8-dab5438a0709" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508476} {:answer/id #uuid "463b2e71-dbe7-52d1-afb3-71d62e0273b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508494} {:answer/id #uuid "a3064872-5e4c-57e5-9d47-2c2deb22dec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508636} {:answer/id #uuid "c3ec6af2-4f1a-52c6-a25e-18c1477fc5d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508693} {:answer/id #uuid "eb3970cd-670c-51c7-b392-e17578742da3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3064872-5e4c-57e5-9d47-2c2deb22dec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508636} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4450d37-cda0-50d9-ad71-0e2c1df13152" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508903}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ec5e8c7c-c10d-59da-bddc-7ee7a7739de6" :question/math-academy-id "q-62062" :question/problem "Joel invested $$11\\,280.$ The investment performed poorly, losing one-eighth of its value every month.\n\nThe function $p(t)$ models the value of the investment after $t$ months and is given by\n\n$$\np(t)=11\\,280\\cdot {(\\text{___})}^{t}.\n$$\n\nWhat number is missing?" :question/worked-solution "The initial investment was $$11\\,280$, and this decreased by $\\frac{1}{8}$ every month.\n\nIf the investment value is reduced by $\\frac{1}{8},$ then $\\frac{7}{8}$ of its value remained every month. So the decay factor is $\\frac{7}{8}.$\n\nThe formula for exponential decay (in terms of a decay factor $b$) is\n\n$$\np=a{b}^{t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- $a=11\\,280$ is the initial investment.\n\n- $b=\\frac{7}{8}$ is the decay factor.\n\n- $t=$ the time, in months.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $p(t)$ is\n\n$$\np(t)=11\\,280\\cdot {(\\frac{7}{8})}^{t}.\n$$\n\nSo the missing number is $\\frac{7}{8}.$"}]}
